NIGHT_LOADED({"seed":1103,"generated_at":"2026-10-21T06:00:00Z","chain":[1,4,2,3,5],"frame":{"collector":"J.D.","intro":["You are the new assistant.","On the table lies a note from the collector.","The key to the front door is in his coat, and he has gone home.","The clock says a quarter past nine.","You begin to sort."],"note_table":"File twelve envelopes.\nCabinet five stays shut.\nLock up before twelve.\n— J.D.","note_final":"Well filed. Tomorrow at nine. — J.D.","card_desk":{"kind":"Legend","description":"In the Central Legend Archive there is a reading table with a green cloth, and on it a lamp with a green shade. Along the wall stand five cabinets with drawers full of cards. In the evening, when the others have gone, the assistant who worked late sits there and reads. Only the hands can be seen in the lamplight.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1936,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","teller":"the previous assistant","note":"Don’t read it. File it."},"trail_notes":["Not recorded by me. My previous assistant.","Same hand. He worked on into the evenings.","His last. No more cards from him after that.","This one he did not file. Nor did I."],"card_five":{"kind":"Legend","description":"There was once a new assistant at the Legend Archive who stayed on one evening to finish the filing. The collector had gone home. The assistant put four cabinets in order and then opened the fifth as well, though it was to stay shut. After that the assistant was never seen again. The cards lay neatly in order, and what the assistant saw there was ____.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":"tomorrow","teller":"J.D.","initials":"J.D.","code":null},"final_words":["nothing","me","myself","the assistant","the previous assistant"],"door_locked":"Locked. The key is in J.D.’s coat.","midnight":"The clock strikes twelve.","good_end":"Well done. Cabinet five stays shut.","nee":"No.","not_yet":"Not yet.","into_envelope":"Into the envelope.","archive_note":"You need not go behind the divider tonight.","finish_first":"Not yet. Cabinet {roman} first.","digit_note":"{n}. The number of cabinet {roman}.","digit_first":"Remember: the lock of cabinet V wants four of these.","found_notes":{"chair":"One is where I put it down yesterday.","lamp":"One is under the lamp. Don’t move the lamp.","coat":"One is in my coat. Leave the coat hanging.","typewriter":"One is still in the machine."},"floor_note":"That one does not belong in that drawer.","machine_continued":"— continued in drawer 3 —","reactions":{"reopen_filed":"That one was done.","stalled":"Hurry up.","read_desk":"I said: don’t read it.","typo3":"It is there. Read.","other_hand":"he is not coming back","five_shut":"Shut."},"citation":"Source: Dutch Folktale Database (Nederlandse Volksverhalenbank), Meertens Institute (KNAW), www.verhalenbank.nl"},"cabinets":[{"id":1,"label":"Omens","digit":9,"drawers":[{"id":"1-1","type":"P4","difficulty":1.5216,"rank":0.092,"note":"Torn in two. The rest is in the box on the table.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"KOOIJMAN1128","role":"top","render":{"description":"Kees Stolwijk says that his wife's father used to live in Honkoop. Once when they were walking somewhere, her father suddenly said","place":"Hoenkoop","prov":"Utr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/72618","half":"top"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ009012","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Three times he is pushed off the road. Finally he is thrown into a ditch. This was done by a funeral procession he was walking in the way of.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0481"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ056404","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"A week later the old woman was sitting outside and again saw a black ribbon. Another week later she died. The black ribbon was the funeral procession. She had seen it in advance.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0486"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ120301","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"It is an omen of his wife's death.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0486"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ025002","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"But there was nothing and no one to be seen. A few days later potatoes were stolen. Then exactly the same rustling could be heard as before.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0487"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"CJ086402","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"He also kept forgetting something, so that he had already gone back home three times. That same week he drowned while swimming.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0486"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"CBAK0030","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"She does see a shade in the form of a dove flying. That must have been an omen of her brother's death a few days later.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0486"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c8","story_id":"GENDT140","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"A few days later the father dies and the neighbours come to pray for the deceased.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0486"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c9","story_id":"WEV015702","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Shortly afterwards a newborn baby dies, neighbours carry the small coffin, and a dog barks.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0486"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c10","story_id":"KOOIJMAN1128","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"that someone had to step aside. They did not want to. He could see what was coming and the others could not. Mrs Stolwijk says that her father called out that they had to step aside, because a funeral procession was coming.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0481"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c11","story_id":"CJ011207","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The neighbour girl says: \"The first one to come out the door will be the one, they say.\" The woman says she hopes it won't be her. A little later the neighbour girl goes to her sister. Her sister's husband has forgotten his work trousers, and the girl takes them after him. She had already caught up with him when she tripped and fell flat on the street. She was dead on the spot.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0486"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c12","story_id":"CJ123403","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Some people also have visions of a fire. Others hear the sound of carpentry at a certain spot, although a house is only built there much later.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0489"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c13","story_id":"CJ076508","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Afterwards he tells everyone never again to walk in the middle of the road in the evening.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0481"},"home":"1-1"}],"hints":["Read the top piece to the last word. What is mentioned already?","The top piece breaks off in mid-sentence. The bottom one finishes it.","The number is SINSAG 0481. There are three with that number in the box."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c10"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c10"],"stack":["c1","c10"]},"found_card":null},{"id":"1-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.3058,"rank":0.6075,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ046312","role":"member","render":{"description":"Never run in the middle of the road at night: a funeral procession may pass.","place":"Surhuisterveen","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24424","original":"Wy woarden altyd warskôge: rin noait midden op 'e wei by joun of by nacht, hwant der kin us in lykstaesje passeare.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ102104","role":"member","render":{"description":"Some people had to get out of bed at night to see funeral processions. You should never run in the middle of the road at night.","place":"Augustinusga","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/37102","original":"Yn 'e Harkema en yn Stiensgea ha 'k wol guon kend dy't nachts fan bêd moesten om lykstaesjes to sjen.\nMen moest nachts noait midden op 'e wei rinne.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"KOOIJMAN2266","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"You were warned not to walk in the cart track or on the bridle path at night. Because there you could meet evil spirits.","place":"Heesselt","prov":"Gld.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0333","initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/127631","original":"Dat weet ik ook nog. Je werd gewaarschuwd om 's nachts niet in 't wagenspoor of in 't paardenpad te lopen. Want daar kon je de boze geesten tegenkomen.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"cab:4"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ052415","role":"member","render":{"description":"The narrator tells of two men who often saw funeral processions. You must never walk in the middle of the road, because an invisible funeral procession can drive you off the road.","place":"Surhuisterveen","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25234","original":"Douwe Stavasius fan Grinzer Pein seach lykstaesjes.\nBoardzer Bruining fan Boelensloane ek. Dy leeft noch.\nMen mat noait midden op 'e wei rinne, hwant der kin us in lykstaesje oankomme, sûnder dat men it sjocht. Dan wurde jo fan 'e wei ôfsmiten.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"}],"hints":["Look at the numbers in red pencil.","Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The card about Heesselt belongs with the Ghosts."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c3","cabinet":4},"on_success":{"trail_note":0,"unlock_cabinet":4,"stack":["c1","c2","c4"]}},{"id":"1-3","type":"R1","difficulty":1.1165,"rank":0.2343,"note":"The clock has stopped. These three know the time.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ011311","role":"omen","render":{"description":"At an empty spot, people often heard hammering in the evening from nine o'clock on. Years later a farm came there.","place":"Boornbergum","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/17750","original":"Yn 'e Surhústermieden by de feart wie in plak, dêr gong it nachts faek op in timmerjen. Njoggen ûre jouns dan bigong it. Altyd klunderen se dêr nachts om. Mar der wie dêrom neat as men der hinne gong.\n\"Hjir komt fêst in hûs\", seinen wy tsjin elkoar.\nIt hat noch jierren duorre, doe is dêr in nij spultsje delset woarn, flak by de brêge.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ096708","role":"omen","render":{"description":"A father and mother had twins. At nine months one of the children fell ill and died. At the churchyard the father said that their other child would die too. He had seen it lying in a little coffin. When they came home the other child had died as well.","place":"Buitenpost","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"SINSAG 0483","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/36140","original":"Heit en mem hienen twillingen. It iene berntsje woarde siik, doe wie 't njoggen maenden âld. It stoar en sy brochten it nei 't hôf ta. Doe sei heit: \"It oare berntsje hâlde wy ek net. Ik ha 't al yn 't kistje lizzen sjoen.\" Doe't se weromkommen fan 't tsjerkhôf wie 't oare berntsje ek dea.\nHeit en mem wennen doe yn 'e Twizeler Mieden.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"WEV011104","role":"omen","render":{"description":"Roosters that crow at nine o'clock in the evening or later predict rain and wind.","place":"Sellingen","prov":"Gr.","year":1965,"code":"TM 4001","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43504","original":"As de hoanen s oavends om n uur of negen of loater nog kraaien, den kriegn ie gauw regen en wind.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"}],"hints":["Read them again. All three count something.","The same number three times. That is the time.","9 o’clock. Set the clock."],"lock":{"kind":"clock_hour","hour":9},"on_success":{"chime":9,"digit":{"value":9,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}}]},{"id":2,"label":"White Women","digit":2,"drawers":[{"id":"2-1","type":"P5","difficulty":0.6258,"rank":0.0,"note":"The tellers contradict each other. Go by the oldest.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"HOL000404","role":"variant","render":{"description":"Seeing a witte juffer (white lady); playing at being a witte juffer with a white sheet around oneself.","place":"Ingen","prov":"Gld.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/209537","original":"Witte vrouwen . Bij de pas (aanplant van wilgen of populieren met onderhout van elzen en essen) (lag dicht bij de woning van de zegslieden) zag men soms een witte gedaante lopen. Maar sommigen geloofden niet aan de witte juffer, zo werd Han Briene er van verdacht, dat hij soms de kinderen bang wilde maken door voor witte juffer te spelen (hij deed zich dan een laken om) Enige jongens wilden met Jas Gaosbeek, een niet volwaardige zoon van een bakker, een grap uithalen. Zij sloegen zich lakens om en gingen wandelen op een plaats, waar Jas passeren moest. Deze ging er echter niet voor door, maar begon de \"juffer\", die hij het eerst te pakken kreeg af te ranselen. De andere jongens sloegen toen op de vlucht","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"HOL002208","role":"variant","render":{"description":"In the evening, mistaking a stick with a newspaper on it for a witte juffer (white lady).","place":"Ochten","prov":"Gld.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210065","original":"Er moet een witte juffer gelopen hebben op het Zand (fruitteeltbedrijf) bij het witte hek (dit stond op de weg, die tussen twee kolken doorloopt. Keuken, hij was toen 18 jaar, ging eens met een kameraad naar Eldik (buurtschap) om een vriend te bezoeken. Deze bleek niet thuis. Op de dijk op de plaats waar beneden het witte hek stond, was een stok met krant er om gezet, als teken voor de castreur dat er \"keujes\" moesten gesneden worden. Janus stapte tegen deze stok aan, deze ging heen en weer, de kameraad beweerde, dat hij een witte juffer had gezien en was van dit idee, ook de volgende dag, niet af te brengen","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"HOL002604","role":"variant","render":{"description":"A white maiden who asks the way throws a hat full of money and disappears.","place":"Tiel","prov":"Gld.","year":1964,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210163","original":"Berend, den dakuil (een Van Uden) smeerde de daken van binnen aan met kalk, vandaar dat hij deze bijnaam kreeg. Eens liep Berend op de Grotebrugse grintweg bij de Twaalf Apostelen (straatje) toen een witte juffer hem de weg vroeg naar het veer. Berend zei haar die en nadat hij dit gedaan had, gooide zij hem de hoed vol met \"Berliner daolder\". Driemaal was Berend dit overkomen. Bij het veer gekomen wilde Berend haar bedanken, maar hij kreeg geen kans daartoe: zij was verdwenen.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":null,"role":"summary","render":{"description":"In Gelderland an object was seen: ____. (according to the oldest recording)","place":null,"year":null,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","summary":true},"home":"2-1"}],"hints":["Look at the years.","The oldest is from 1962.","That card names an object. Which?"],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"67d7e2afbf01cfe8","accepted_hashes":["18217f3045257440bd9a07cb559aecc81e17b50bc72d521c10b2b9b0bcb4edd6","251aa74f07de082167c4d7bcc7ae204283bd5cf2ceeeb2b118f1789b2ee87ebd","50f72a299fe7952cbdc6441ec8563409c4c0ad6caac2e45f192384b8c6772d26","d0cac78482ef4f07ed19803b282bd20e48bb8fda970acea9ca05b2c732de505d","da7d3ddd596649461dd07669acdc2cca27144d2f4a26ff4a6267af4451e0d40b","e10f934e68988a1ef760556e6d13783090de71a75e1aa0a8bf54cf03d8e15bfa"],"fill":"c4"},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c4","field":"blank","value":"typed"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"2-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.2246,"rank":0.733,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ009417","role":"member","render":{"description":"In the past witte wieven (white women) were often seen at night in Westerein.","place":"De Westereen","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/17488","original":"Froeger waerden der wol wite wiven sjoen nachts yn 'e Westerein.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"KOOIJMAN1426","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"Strange people were said to dress up as a werewolf.","place":"Woudrichem","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1963,"code":null,"initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/125543","original":"In mijn jeugd ging het verhaal van de weerwolf, da 't toen zo was, da vreemde mense zich verkleed hadde. Dan sprake ze van de weerwolf.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ007910","role":"member","render":{"description":"In the lane by Hattum de Vries a wit wijf (white woman) always haunted at night. People did not dare go there at night, because the white woman drove them to the side towards the little lake. Without doing anything themselves, they ended up in the lake.","place":"Oudega","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/17053","original":"By Hattum de Vries yn it loantsje spoeke nachts altyd in wyt wiif. De minsken doarsten dêr nachts noait to kommen. Hwant sy waerden dêr stadich troch dat wite wiif oan kant treaun nei de dobbe ta. Sûnder dat se it sels fornamen kommen se yn 'e dobbe torjochte.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"DYKFRIES2187","role":"member","render":{"description":"In the time of Emperor Lothair, many witte wijven (white women) lived in Friesland. These were malicious spirits and ghosts that carried people and children off to their lair. Later these beings were called witte juffers (white ladies), but these were friendly and helpful by nature.","place":"Goutum","prov":"Fr.","year":1896,"code":null,"initials":"W.D.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/69790","original":"Ten tijde van keizer Lotharius werd men in Friesland veel geplaagd door geesten en spoken. Zij woonden op de spits van een kleinen heuvel in een kunstig hol, dat door geen menschenhanden was gemaakt. Gewoonlijk werden zij witte wijven genoemd. Aangaande hare uiterlijke gedaante wist men niet veel. Nachtelijke wandelaars, veehoeders, vrouwen en kinderen werden dikwijls door deze witte wijven weggevoerd naar hare holen en onderaardsche gangen. Daaruit hoorde men niet zelden zuchten, snikken en kindergeschrei. Zorgvuldig bewaakte men daarom zwangere vrouwen en kinderen, opdat dezen niet door de witte vrouwen zouden worden weggehaald. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a werewolf.","The card about Woudrichem belongs with the Werewolves."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c2","cabinet":3},"on_success":{"trail_note":2,"unlock_cabinet":3,"stack":["c1","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"2-3","type":"R2","difficulty":1.0511,"rank":0.5424,"note":"Something is written on the window. Don’t wipe it off.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"LAAN004a","role":"card","render":{"description":"Dr. Wumkes tells where Widde Wieven (white women) have been seen. They were seen near Enum, at Krewerd and on the road to Arwerd. They preferred strange places. On the border of Slochteren and Schildwolde they walked up and down an oak avenue in long white robes. They were never seen by day, but they were not afraid. They were in eerie places and in churchyards. They were also always at places where something had happened.","place":"Lellens","prov":"Gr.","year":1930,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"E.F.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/42287","original":"Widde Juvvers\n\nWidde Wieven zijn overal; bij nacht en ontijd zweven zij langs lanen en wegen. Dr. Wumkes vertelt, dat zij gezien zijn op de börgstee van Alberda bij Enum; te Krewerd boeten 't loug op de weg naar Arwerd. Zij hadden voorkeur voor buitengewone plaatsen: een brug of vonder, een kruisweg, een wierde. Op de grens van Slochteren en Schildwolde wandelden ze een eikenlaan op en neer in lange, witte gewaden bij avond of nacht. Over dag heeft nooit iemand er een gezien. Bang zijn ze niet; ze duren wel op de griezelkste steden, alderdeegs op 't kerkhòf wel.\nOok zijn ze altijd op plaatsen, doar wat gebeurd is, zo op 't Huis de Wolf tussen Stad en Haren, en ook bij Den Andel.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ057303","role":"sill","render":{"description":"Several people have seen two witte wijven (white women) in the woods.","place":"Opende","prov":"Gr.","year":1969,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25852","stain":"two"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ020717","role":"card","render":{"description":"A man once saw a white lady during a polecat hunt.","place":"Harkema","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20675","original":"Wy ha wol us to murdzjen west. Doe ha wy in kear in wite juffer by de ikene beam sjoen.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"ENGELB_15_003","role":"card","render":{"description":"About the existence of witte wieven (white women) and the spit in the doorpost.","place":"Geesteren","prov":"Ov.","year":1979,"code":"SINSAG 0161","initials":"H.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/128566","original":"H.E.: Van de witn wiew he’j doar wa mangs van heurd?\nVr.Vr.: Van de witn wiew is ok niks van woar.\nH.E.: Nee, mer te geet ok um t verhaal, he. Joa he’j hier nog zonnen beuld, zonnen witn wievnbeuld. Ne, nee, nee (door elkaar heen gepraat, ze zijn het met elkaar niet eens)\nVr. [Wolberink, Jan]: Wat hadn ze bie ouns ok zegd, oh jee no valt mie t kenneke in zee Dat stun nog moal vuur joarn in de Twentse kraant. Als ik t met ene schoen had vastgebondn, gevondn als de ander gebondn.\nA.Ve.: ... t spit nog in n stiel van n nienduur nog zitn.\nF.Ve.: t Spit brengn.","lang":"Twente dialect","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CBOEK305","role":"card","render":{"description":"Another ghost story tells of a lady in a white veil who comes through the wall between twelve and one o'clock. If anyone disturbs her rest, she wrings his neck. A strong man goes to the castle she haunts at night and destroys her for good.","place":"Driebergen-Rijsenburg","prov":"Utr.","year":1892,"code":"SINSAG 0301","initials":"M.R.v.d.V.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/34810","original":"Een Spookgeschiedenis\nEen spookgeschiedenis zooals deze is er nog een, waarin eene geheimzinnige witgesluierde Dame het spook is; welke eveneens tusschen 12 en 1 uur komt, maar door den muur heen in de slaapkamer en roept, (wanneer zij iemand in de kamer ziet, welke het spook dooden wil), met een holle, nare grafstem: \"Wie stoort hier mijn rust?\" Daarop loopt zij toornig op den bevenden man toe en draait hem den hals om; daarna verdwijnt zij weer door den muur, alhoewel er geen deur in is. Nu durft niemand meer te wagen op het kasteel een nacht te slapen; totdat er eindelijk een moedige sterken man komt, op 't slot des nachts gaat en de witte Dame voor altijd verdelgt...\n(Breedvoerig ken ik deze historie niet meer.)","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"EGGEN001705","role":"card","render":{"description":"Meeting a white woman floating through the air.","place":"Berg","prov":"L.","year":1970,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"C.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/207880","original":"Onderwerp : wit wijf.\nTijd : einde 19de eeuw\nPlaats : Berg.\n\nIch weit noch, tot in daen tiēd mèr 'n paar hoezer in Berg sjtonge. En dao op Bemele aan, al gaar gein.\nOppenen aovend, heldere maon, gein mis of gèt, kaom 'n oud vruike nao hoēs, in Berg.\nMèh zie waor kaom aan 't begin van de grwoatstraot (grote straat), dao huërt zie geroēsj in de buim langs de weeg. Dao waor geine wind, en toch roēsjden 't. Zie kraog al gèt angs, en wol vlot wiejer loupe, pes aan de hoezer.\nMèh zie haet nog kaom eine sjtap gezat, dao kump 'n wit wiēf aangezwaef door de loch, zwoa grwoat wie 'ne wollek. \nZie ging rech-op van den angs.\nDoe die versjiening euver waor, leep dat auw minsjke wat 't loupe kòs, nao 't iërsjte hoēs.\nEn van dao haet me hör nao hoēs gebrach.","lang":"Limburgish","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"}],"hints":["Read it from back to front.","It begins with O.","Opende. Lay that card on the windowsill."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c2","object":"window","text":"Opende"},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":2,"card":"c2","word":"two","stained":"c2"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6"]}}]},{"id":3,"label":"Werewolves","digit":7,"drawers":[{"id":"3-1","type":"P1","difficulty":1.1309,"rank":0.9121,"note":"All four name the same thing. That becomes the label. Don’t write ‘a beast’.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"EDJSL003","role":"card","render":{"description":"A farmhand tells his girl that he has an errand to run, and that if she meets a vicious dog she must give it her handkerchief. She does indeed meet a dog, throws the handkerchief at it and flees. During the meal it is seen that he has pieces of a handkerchief between his teeth. When his room is searched, the belt that turns someone into a werewolf is found. As soon as the belt is thrown into the fire, the farmhand, who was working far away, is standing by the oven trying to jump into the fire. After the belt has burned, the farmhand is released.","place":"Bladel","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1894,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"E.d.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/9505","original":"De weerwolf\nEr was eens een boerenknecht die soms een weerwolf was.\nDe knecht vrijde met een van de meiden, maar zij wist van de prins geen kwaad. Op een keer waren ze een eind buiten het dorp gaan wandelen. Toen ze op huis aangingen, viel de schemer in.\nOpeens had de knecht zin weerwolf te worden.\nHij zei tegen de meid: \"Ik moet hier even een boodschap doen. Loop jij maar vast door, ik haal je wel in. Mocht je een kwade hond tegenkomen, die je wil bijten, gooi hem dan mijn zakdoek toe. Dan heeft hij iets om zijn tanden in te zetten, terwijl jij ervandoor gaat.\"\nHij ging weg, en een poosje later zag ze een grote hond op zich afkomen. Ze gooide hem de zakdoek toe en zette het op een lopen. Het dier scheurde de zakdoek aan flarden en at hem op. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"BOEKV179","role":"card","render":{"description":"A youth is a werewolf. When he is walking with his girl, he feels that he is about to change. He sends her on ahead and warns her about a big dog. She must throw her handkerchief to it, and then the girl can flee. Later, however, she and her family see the pieces of handkerchief between the youth's teeth. Werewolves always wear a band around their waist. The farmer the youth works for burns the band. The werewolf still tries to get into the fire, but he is held back. When the band has burned, the youth is an ordinary person again.","place":"Bladel","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1896,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"G.J.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35060","original":"Van een Weerwolf.\n\nOp de Achterste hoef woonde indertijd een boer, en die boer had een knecht, en dat was een weerwolf. Op een eigenaardige manier zijn ze daar achter gekomen.\nDie knecht vrijde met een meid uit de buurt. Eens waren die twee samen buiten dorps (1) geweest en 't was al tusschen licht en donker toen ze op huis aan gingen. Ze waren al niet meer zoo heel ver van huis toen voelde hij een onweerstaanbare lust om weerwolf te worden; maar de meid merkte het natuurlijk niet. Hij zei tot haar: \"Ik moet hier eens effekens (2) van den weg af bij genen boer zijn; ga gij maar door: ik zal u wel inhalen. Maar komt ge soms een kwaden hond tegen, die op u aan bijt, gooit hem dan mijn zakdoek toe; dien zal hij misschien wel vatten. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"SINBRABSAG185","role":"card","render":{"description":"A young man is a werewolf. When he is walking with his girl, he feels that he is about to change. He sends her on ahead and warns her about a big dog. She must throw her handkerchief to it, and then the girl can flee. Later, however, she and her family see the pieces of handkerchief between the young man's teeth. This is how they know he is a werewolf.","place":"Bladel","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1933,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"I.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/46940","original":"No. 185. Op de Achterste hoef bij Bladel woonde indertijd een boer, en die boer had een knecht, en dat was een weerwolf. Op 'n vreemde manier zijn ze dat aan de weet gekomen. Die knecht vrijde met een meid uit de buurt. Eens waren die twee samen buitendorps geweest en 't was al tusschen licht en donker, toen ze op huis aan gingen. Ze waren al niet ver meer van huis toen hij een onweerstaanbaren lust voelde om weerwolf te worden; maar de meid merkte dat natuurlijk niet. Hij zei tot haar: \"Ik moet hier eens effekens van den weg af bij genen boer zijn, ga gij maar door: ik zal oe wel inhalen. Maar komt ge soms een kwaden hond tegen, die naar oe bijt, gooit hem dan mijn zakdoek toe; dien zal hij wel vatten. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"LYST009","role":"card","render":{"description":"A couple go for a walk in the evening. The boy has to relieve himself, but before he disappears into the bushes he advises the girl that if a beast attacks her, she should throw her handkerchief in front of its mouth. A dangerous beast does indeed come at the girl. She throws her handkerchief in front of its jaws and the beast tears it apart. When the boy comes back, the girl sees that he has remnants of her handkerchief between his teeth. She now knows he is a werewolf and tells him so. The boy disappears and never came back.","place":"Erp","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1953,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"F.W.J.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13223","original":"De Weerwolf\nEen vrijer bracht 's avonds z'n meisje naar huis. Onderweg zei ie: \"Ik moet even mijn behoefte doen. Als je in tussentijd een dier of zoiets op je af ziet komen, gooi het dan je zakdoek voor z'n kop.\" Toen de jongen weg was, kwam er een dier op het meisje aangelopen. Ze slingerde haar zakdoek voor z'n muil en het beest verscheurde hem. Even later kwam de jongen terug en hij vroeg zijn meisje of er iets gebeurd was. Ze vertelde wat er was voorgevalllen en terwijl keek ze hem strak aan. Toen zei ze hem: \"Ik geloof, dat jij het beest bent geweest, want je hebt de stukken zakdoek nog tussen je tanden zitten\" Onmiddellijk was de vrijer verdwenen, en het meisje heeft hem nooit teruggezien.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"}],"hints":["Read the four again. Look at what occurs in each of the four, not at what happens in them.","It is an object.","Begins with H. 12 letters."],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"67d7e2afbf01cfe8","accepted_hashes":["3f73c212f00bb69f122990ca3ce45f341e06c5ce1cdeeaf64233ebb035b52fde","901fcbf317c4b018ef8441720af2012bb45f478ae8684f4b8c8b5686f7a9d5ac","a8767ed0bed9b073c5d08662987b99dbe66c8db8cfdfbda097baff1a7a9de619","de735a4b3b5e484739e4b4490507b1ae9096fb75b49e48102946e00cd4ff11c7"]},"on_success":{"print_label":true,"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c4"}},{"id":"3-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.3078,"rank":0.9137,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ084112","role":"member","render":{"description":"One of seven girls is a nightmare and one of seven boys is a werewolf.","place":"Rottevalle","prov":"Fr.","year":1971,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/32830","original":"Se sizze fan 'e sawn famkes út ien húshâlding is ien in nachtmerje en fan 'e sawn jonges út in húshâlding is ien in wearwolf","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ101519","role":"member","render":{"description":"One of seven daughters is a nightmare; one of seven sons is a werewolf.","place":"Drachtstercompagnie","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/36981","original":"Ien fan sawn famkes út ien gesin wie in nachtmerje.\nIen fan sawn jonges út ien gesin wie in wjerwolf.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ085401","role":"member","render":{"description":"One of seven brothers is a werewolf. When he has one of his fits, you must throw him an old apron or something like it. He then tears it to pieces. If you see someone with threads hanging from his mouth, you can be sure he is a werewolf.","place":"Rottevalle","prov":"Fr.","year":1971,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/33002","original":"In wearwolf is in minske, dy forropt de boel. 't Is ien fan sawn jonges (7 bruorren). As er wer sa'n kuer krijt, dat er hwat forskuorre mat, mat men him in âld skelk of sahwathinne tasmite. Us mem sei, dan gebeurde 't wol dat him even letter de triedden ta de mûle úthongen.\nAs men sa'n ien seach, dy't triedden ta de mûle út hie, koe men der fan op oan dat it in wearwolf wie. Dêr koe men se oan herkenne.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"HOL001916","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"Acquainted with people who can turn into werewolves; a woman sees a werewolf or the devil.","place":"Maurik","prov":"Gld.","year":1963,"code":null,"initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/209980","original":"Men wist nog wel mensen te noemen, die de naam hadden te kunnen weerwolven. Wat ze deden, wist men niet.\nDe \"aauwe\" Roel moest de weerwolf of was het \"den duvel\" verdrijven. Zij zag hem komen en schreeuwde 's nachts: \"Daor heddum al weer\" (moet in Ingen gebeurd zijn, de \"aauwe\" Roel was de buurvrouw.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:5"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about the devil.","The card about Maurik belongs with the Devil."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c4","cabinet":5},"on_success":{"trail_note":3,"unlock_cabinet":5,"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}},{"id":"3-3","type":"R3","difficulty":1.111,"rank":0.8462,"note":"When someone knocks: count. That card under the door.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ071510","role":"door","render":{"description":"A werewolf is a young man who rides a horse. He torments the horse just as a nightmare torments a person. He is one of seven brothers.","place":"Rohel","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":"TM 3107","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/28067","original":"In wjerwolf is in manspersoan, - meastal in jongkeardel -, dy't op in hynder rydt. Hy pleaget dat hynder, krekt as in nachtmerje de minsken. 't Is ien fan sawn bruorren. Ik ha wol ien kend, dy wenne yn Warffum.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ071310","role":"card","render":{"description":"One of eight sons was a werewolf. A werewolf could never eat his fill; he was always still hungry.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/28045","original":"As der acht jonges wienen, dy't op elkoar folgen yn in húshâlding, dan wie ien fan dy acht in wjerwolf. Dat wie ien dy't noait sêd koe, dy't neat fan ûnpas kom.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"VVUNL049","role":"card","render":{"description":"Every evening after dinner Sjang goes out and does not come back until very late. One time they follow him and see him take something out of a tree, and a moment later he was a werewolf. The priest is fetched and Sjang has to produce his things. Out came a sheepskin and a red stick with a red ribbon; these are burnt in the oven while three men hold Sjang down. When everything is charred, he says he is freed.","place":"Kessel","prov":"L.","year":1952,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"J.N.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35588","original":"De geplaagde herder \n\n't Gebeurde op 'Gravenhof' te Kessel, tussen 1860 en '70. Sjang van de Maas uit Neer was hier scheper; een onnozele, rustige kerel, die niemand kwaad deed, en elke dag zijn schapen hoedde. Maar na een tijdje maakten de boer en de boerin zich over hem ongerust. Elke avond na het eten verdween Sjang plotseling en keerde pas heel laat in de nacht weer huiswaarts. Dit werd zo verdacht dat men op een keer de knaap stilletjes achtervolgde... Men zag toen dat hij tot de holle boom liep, even voorbij het Annakapelletje; daar nam hij iets uit. Na enkele ogenblikken veranderde hij van gedaante, en stoof als schrikaanjagende weerwolf met een geweldige vaart weg. . . …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"LYST008","role":"card","render":{"description":"Every night at exactly twelve o'clock a farmhand takes a small hoop out of the lime tree. He hangs the hoop around his neck and turns into a werewolf. He roams about for a while and tears apart everything that comes near him. After that he becomes an ordinary person again. The farmer finds his behaviour strange and asks the priest for advice. The priest realises that the farmhand is a werewolf and advises the farmer to send the farmhand on an errand from which he can never be back home by midnight. On the agreed night the priest takes the hoop out of the tree at midnight. The farmhand is standing under that tree and sees everything. He flees and never comes back.","place":"Erp","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1953,"code":"SINSAG 0803","initials":"F.W.J.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13222","original":"De Weerwolf\nEen boerenknecht kroop 's nachts klokslag 12 uur in de lindenboom voor de boerderij. Boven in de boom hing voor gewone mensen onzichtbaar een hoepeltje. Dat hing de knecht om zijn hals. Als ie uit de boom geklauterd was, liep ie in de gedaante van een hond weg en verscheurde alles wat hem in de weg kwam. Als ie een tijd zo rondgelopen had, was ie weer gewoon mens. Na een tijd was het de boer, bij wie de weerwolf in dienst was, opgevallen, dat zijn knecht nacht op nacht weg was. Hij ging naar de pastoor en die had het zaakje meteen door. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"TINNEV042","role":"card","render":{"description":"Two men are looking for grass stalks to cut. When they find none, they go home. After they have parted, one of the men suddenly sees a large wolf on his path. The next morning the other man asks him whether he saw the wolf.","place":"Didam","prov":"Gld.","year":1944,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"A.T.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22388","original":"29.\nPeter ging op een kier met Dorus mieskes sni'je. Mao zi'j konne de gin vinne en wolle daorum weer op huus aan. De weg liep deur een buske. Dorus vroeg aan Peter offe um nao huus sol brenge. \"Loop nao da galg\", antwore Peter en kroap onder de scheibeum nève de weg hèèr.\n\"Hi'j is ter\", riep Dorus um nao. Ienéns stong d'r een grote wolf op de bosweg. Hi'j wol niet op zied gaon. Daorum drèèje Peter de met een flinken boag umhen. Toe e is umkek zag e niks meer. Umdat Peter geld neudig had ginge de 's marges weer op uut um smele te zuke. Ien Kilder was Dorus al met een groten trop aan 't sni'je. Toe hi'j Peter zag riep tem toe: \"Wasse d'r now, of niet?\".","lang":"Liemers dialect","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"}],"hints":["Wait for the knocking. Count it.","An odd number.","7 times. That card."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c1","object":"door","n":7},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":7,"card":"c2"},"stack":["c2","c3","c4","c5"]}}]},{"id":4,"label":"Ghosts","digit":3,"drawers":[{"id":"4-1","type":"P2","difficulty":3.1343,"rank":0.2092,"note":"No place. Somewhere between the other three. Pin it on the map.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"KOOIJMAN2326","role":"target","render":{"description":"In the old days people sometimes saw a wagon with two horses driving through the air. This was also said during thunderstorms.","place":null,"prov":"Gld.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0478","initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/127722"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"KOOIJMAN1559","role":"helper","render":{"description":"At night people saw a rider on a horse flying through the air.","place":"Culemborg","prov":"Gld.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0478","initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/125747","original":"Dat ze 's nachts een ruiter te paard door de lucht hadden zien vliegen.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"4-1","geo":[51.955,5.22778]},{"id":"c3","story_id":"HOL002513","role":"helper","render":{"description":"Haunting on farms; in the evening the threshing machine and winnowing mill run.","place":"Kapel-Avezaath","prov":"Gld.","year":1964,"code":"SINSAG 0478","initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210140","original":"Op de boerderij bij de dames Versteeg spookte het. (Dit was op Aldenhaaf, zie opname Koehein). Op Teisterbant was het vroeger soms helemaal mis. Er woonde daar toen een Versteeg. 's Avonds hoorde men de dorsmolen lopen, ook de wanmolen en de hakselmachine (Men sprak van \"kortsnijmachine\", ook bij mij thuis). Den knecht zei tegen Versteeg: \"Laote we der een paor gaarven deur gooie, want de mesine lop toch\" \nHierop wilde Versteeg toch niet ingaan (zie opname Van Zijtveld)","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"4-1","geo":[51.88,5.37639]},{"id":"c4","story_id":"HOL002610","role":"helper","render":{"description":"Ghosts turn out to be escaped calves.","place":"Tiel","prov":"Gld.","year":1964,"code":"SINSAG 0478","initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210169","original":"Een neef van grootvader Boudewijn bracht eens, het was met Tielse kermis, een meisje naar huis. In Wadenoijen bij de Pijpekasten werd het meisje bang (die Pijpekasten was een rij huisjes heb ik begrepen). Ook een paar andere kermisgangers durfden niet verder te lopen, want zij zagen daar dingen springen. (Het was een donkere avond). Neef Boudewijn ging er moedig op af. En wat was het geval. Er liepen twee kalveren op de weg. Die waren uit hun wei gegaan.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"4-1","geo":[51.88667,5.42917]}],"hints":["Three places are there already. The fourth lies between them.","Within 2 hours’ walk of Culemborg.","Find Deil on the map."],"lock":{"kind":"place","target_geo":[51.88417,5.24306],"radius_km":6.0},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c1","field":"place","value":"Deil"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c4"}},{"id":"4-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.212,"rank":0.7143,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ015603","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"A fisherman sees a lady in white clothes and decides to follow her. But the wit wief (white woman) vanishes as quickly as she appeared.","place":"Broeksterwâld","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/19893","original":"Douwe syn broer Anne Feddema hie to fiskjen west. Hy hie nei 't tichtset ta west en farde de Lyts út wei werom de kant nei de brêge út. Doe kom der in juffer oan yn sniewite klean. Hy tocht: Ik wol wite hwer't dy keart, dat hy hie 't eech net fan har ôf. Doe't er oan har ta wie, died er de fêstsetter yn 'e kant en krekt doe't er dat die, wie de wite juffer fuort.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"DYKFRIES2153","role":"member","render":{"description":"A glowing foal haunted the Leppedijk. A farm girl had stayed in the village until late and had to go home alone. When she was warned about the ghost foal, she claimed she would put her garter in its mouth and ride it home. But when she actually met the animal, she was terrified and ran home.","place":"Goutum","prov":"Fr.","year":1896,"code":null,"initials":"W.D.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/69329","original":"Op den Leppedijk, niet ver van Oldeboorn, spookte voorheen een gloeiend veulen. Eene boerenmeid was op zekeren avond wat laat in het dorp gebleven en toen haar gezegd werd, dat het veulen haar wel kon ontmoeten, zei ze, dat zij hem dan haar kouseband in den bek zou doen en op hem naar huis rijden. Maar toen zij, op den weg gekomen, het veulen eensklaps vóór zich zag met den bek wijd opengesperd, toen liep zij zoo hard zij kon om tehuis te komen.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"DYKFRIES2191","role":"member","render":{"description":"If someone walked there at night, he might unexpectedly see a white foal racing past him at full speed, after which it suddenly vanished.","place":"Goutum","prov":"Fr.","year":1896,"code":null,"initials":"W.D.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/69795","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"DYKFRIES2156","role":"member","render":{"description":"A farmer from Westdongeradeel regularly encountered a plaaggeest (tormenting spirit). The animal always walked home with him but did him no further harm. The farmer made sure he could always offer the animal a piece of rye bread. His maidservant claimed she would be braver and that if she met the animal, she would ride home on it. When she once met the animal, it put its front paws on her shoulders, so that the maid was forced to carry the animal's weight on her way home.","place":"Goutum","prov":"Fr.","year":1896,"code":null,"initials":"W.D.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/69345","original":"In Westdongeradeel woonde weleer een boer die veel last had van een plaagbeest. Was de man 's avonds bij duister op weg naar zijn huis, dan kwam hem meest altijd zulk een spookdier op zijde. Het vergezelde hem tot aan zijn erf. Eens zelfs was het meegegaan over het bruggetje, dat aan den weg over de gracht lag. Maar dat was dan ook alles; eigenlijk kwaad deed het hem niet. Hij zorgde altijd een stuk roggebrood bij zich te hebben, waarop hij 't beest dan onthaalde. Dit scheen daar smaak in te vinden, nam het gretig aan en liet den boer ongedeerd. Maar de man was toch altijd ontsteld als hij in huis kwam. Zijne dienstmeid vond dit wel wat dwaas en schroomde ook niet voor hare meening uit te komen. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a white woman.","The card about Broeksterwâld belongs with the White Women."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c1","cabinet":2},"on_success":{"trail_note":1,"unlock_cabinet":2,"stack":["c2","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"4-3","type":"R4","difficulty":1.1317,"rank":0.4167,"note":"When the machine starts: let it type to the end. The rest is in here.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"KEMP322","role":"top","render":{"description":"A woman always meets an apparition in a field. On a clergyman's advice she once asks him what he wants.","place":"Broek","prov":"L.","year":1925,"code":"SINSAG 0402","initials":"I.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43449","half":"top"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ112316","role":"half","render":{"description":"When someone tries to pull the chest up, it keeps sinking deeper into the ground. Long ago a gentleman was murdered at that place. He is said to still haunt it.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ053307","role":"half","render":{"description":"When his heirs fail to bury him in that spot, the farmer's ghost keeps wandering. When the farmer is finally buried by the post, the haunting ends.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0402"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"KEMP325","role":"half","render":{"description":"Now, when he comes back from the inn in the evening, a strange figure strikes him in the face. A clergyman tells him to have a holy Mass said and to watch what happens at the consecration. And the boy then sees his mother! He remembers his neglect and makes amends. Since then he has not been troubled by the apparition.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0402"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ069906","role":"half","render":{"description":"At night they always heard noises there; the murdered people were haunting it. In the end the occupants became so frightened that they moved away.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"KEMP322","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"During his life the spirit neglected a pilgrimage, and if the woman makes it for him, he will be released. The woman does so, and the spirit then prays so powerfully for her soul that she died after only three months.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0402","stain":"three"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"BLECOURTNB0007","role":"half","render":{"description":"places is that after his death he must wander with a glowing head at the place where he dared to swear the oath.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-3"}],"hints":["Read what the machine has typed, to the last word.","The rest mentions ‘woman’ again.","The number is SINSAG 0402. There are only three in the envelope."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c6","object":"typewriter"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c6"],"type_line":"Told by: the previous assistant.","digit":{"value":3,"card":"c1","word":"three","stained":"c6"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6","c7"]}}]},{"id":5,"label":"The Devil","digit":null,"drawers":[]}]});
